# ===========================================================================
# Keep the build context small.
#
# Without this file Docker would send the entire project folder to the
# daemon - including the reference projects and the .git directory.
# The installation package (770 MB) is deliberately NOT excluded; the
# Dockerfiles need it.
# ===========================================================================

# Exclude everything ...
*

# ... and whitelist what the builds need.
!docker/
!installer/*.zip
!installer/*.jar

# data/ stays OUT on purpose: no Dockerfile copies from it, everything
# goes through bind mounts. In the context, every change to an XML file
# in data/objects would alter the context hash and needlessly trigger
# the builds - plus a lot of transfer to the daemon for plugin ZIPs.
